/-!
# Exceptional whole-core reconstruction on the original Sylow source

The original Sylow witness removes the plane image. In the surviving Borel
image, the critical-path argument retains the original graph, both full
moving covers, central attachments and all actual transporters. It excludes
all distances above four, then supplies opposed full spans, Baumann control
and the fixed-codimension bound at distance four.

The terminal action uses the even preimage with its genuine quotient 3.A6
modulo the original two-core. This retains the cubic projection kernel E and
its odd quotient E/Q. The two actual moving-quotient models give the final
contradiction, so the original relative commutator core is exhausted by its
central-omega movement.

Faithful FF recognition now proves all five clauses on the whole intrinsic
blockU: elementary abelianness, two-core centrality, irreducibility, order
2^6 and full centralizer equal to the two-core. These supply exceptional
AlternatingSixReconstruction and the unchanged RankTwoAlternatives on the
literal c.L,d.S pair. The natural center-zero branch is a separate source
argument.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 15.3.26--31 and C.1.31--32; Meierfrankenfeld--
Stellmacher (1993), (5.4)--(5.12) and Section 7, printed pp.915--927,932--933.
-/

public noncomputable section
open Subgroup Theory.GroupTheory
open Stellmacher.PushingUp.AmalgamGraph
open CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterC.BinaryMS.MS93
open CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterC.BinaryMS.MS93.DistanceEight.PathCentrality
open CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterC.NaturalSixControl.SymplecticSetup
open Theory.SpecificGroups.SymmetricSix Theory.SpecificGroups.SymmetricSix.BinaryFlags
