/-- The literal original source supplies the full restricted-kernel
configuration of MS93 (5.10). Normalization gives the opposite-mover core
containment; failure gives a nonzero kernel line and central generation
at every component vertex. The actual span's edge intersection is central
at all three starts. The nonnormalizing branch remains to be excluded. -/
theorem source_borel_terminal_kernel_dichotomy
    (hb : 4 < sourceDistance hms)
    {a a' : Vertex Rg} (p : CriticalPath Rg (sourceGeometry hms) a a') :
    ∃ (q : OriginalSylow.BorelBackwardShift (h := hms) p)
      (r : OriginalSylow.BorelBackwardShift (h := hms) q.path)
